## Why This Is Asked
Introduces real-world API auth lifecycle basics and common beginner pitfalls: token expiry, refresh, revocation, and multi-tenant isolation.

## Key Concepts
- OAuth 2.0 token flows (client_credentials, refresh)
- Token expiry handling and refresh race conditions
- Per-tenant data access and scope validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-test snippet: fetch token then call API
async function test() {
  const token = await getToken('client_credentials');
  const res = await fetch('/portfolio', {headers: {Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`}});
  // assert on res.status === 200 and data shape
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate token revocation in CI? 
- How would you add PKCE for public clients and test rotation?

